  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If one root of a quadratic equation is of the form\r\n$a+i b,$ then other root will be $a-i b$ So, all the roots are $2 \\pm 1, \\sqrt{5} \\pm 2 i$\r\n$\\therefore$ Product of all the roots $=(2+i)(2-i)(\\sqrt{5}+2 i)(\\sqrt{5}-2 i)$\r\n$=(4+1)(5+4)=5 \\times 9=45$",
